        "exam_year": "2001",
        "question_text": "<p>Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3} + 2}$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, $\\sqrt{3} - 2$:<br>$\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3} + 2} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 2}{\\sqrt{3} - 2} = \\frac{5(\\sqrt{3} - 2)}{(\\sqrt{3})^2 - (2)^2} = \\frac{5(\\sqrt{3} - 2)}{3 - 4} = \\frac{5(\\sqrt{3} - 2)}{-1} = -5\\sqrt{3} + 10$.</p>",
